      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "The paper mentioned that we prepended a special token as puzzle-id embedding. As puzzle-id is randomly sampled, and the embedding size is large compared to batch size, making it sparse. Thus, AdamW momentums are near zero, essentially reducing to SignSGD. Directly implementing as SignSGD saves compute and VRAM.",
