  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "The paper does not mention the Sparse Embedding trained with SignSGD. The code says \"Adam ≈ SignSGD if gradient is very sparse\", but why would the embedding of the puzzle-id be sparse? And why not use Adam if its approximately equivalent to SignSGD when the embedding is sparse?  \n\nCould you share a paper that document the benefit of SignSGD for embeddings or was this found to slightly improve performance from hyperparameter-tuning?",
